From 0202d2f4f5cdee271dde67e4be46901f2eb5dc56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 19:19:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xfrm: force dst refcount before transport-mode async reinject

The inbound transport-mode async-decap path defers post-decryption
processing to a workqueue via xfrm_trans_queue. The work item runs
under local_bh_disable() but without an explicit rcu_read_lock, so
under CONFIG_PROVE_LOCKING the downstream skb_dst_force() called from
__xfrm_route_forward trips:

  WARNING: include/net/dst.h:317 skb_dst_force.isra.0
  Workqueue: events xfrm_trans_reinject
   skb_dst_force.isra.0+0x38/0x84
   __xfrm_route_forward+0x9c/0x144
   ip_forward+0x410/0x7c0
   xfrm4_rcv_encap_finish2+0x30/0x40
   xfrm_trans_reinject+0xec/0x134

The skb arrives with a noref dst when nf_nat_ipv4_pre_routing
(net/netfilter/nf_nat_proto.c:656) drops the original refcounted dst
on daddr rewrite, and xfrm4_rcv_encap_finish then calls
ip_route_input_noref to re-resolve. The noref dst then crosses the
workqueue boundary.

Convert the dst to refcounted at xfrm_trans_queue_net, the choke
point for both IPv4 and IPv6 transport-mode reinject. All current
callers are inside xfrm_input's outer rcu_read_lock so this is safe.
Per-packet WARN cost is multi-millisecond from dump_stack to the UART
console; under TCP load the retransmit cascade collapses throughput
to zero. Same shape as 3bc07321ccc2 for the analogous crypto-async
boundary one layer up.

Reproducer: LAN host pings via DUT through a transport-mode IPsec
tunnel with MASQUERADE/conntrack on the WAN side; reply path triggers
NAT daddr rewrite + decrypt-then-forward.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
 net/xfrm/xfrm_input.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/xfrm/xfrm_input.c b/net/xfrm/xfrm_input.c
index b91fd2911cf3..f6f1c4ef2584 100644
--- a/net/xfrm/xfrm_input.c
+++ b/net/xfrm/xfrm_input.c
@@ -800,6 +800,30 @@ int xfrm_trans_queue_net(struct net *net, struct sk_buff *skb,
 	if (skb_queue_len(&trans->queue) >= READ_ONCE(net_hotdata.max_backlog))
 		return -ENOBUFS;
 
+	/* On the inbound transport-mode async-decap path, the skb may
+	 * arrive here with a noref dst (e.g. when nf_nat_ipv4_pre_routing
+	 * dropped the original after a daddr rewrite and a subsequent
+	 * ip_route_input_noref re-resolved it). The work item later runs
+	 * in workqueue context with only local_bh_disable(), where the
+	 * rcu_read_lock_held() check inside skb_dst_force() returns false
+	 * under PROVE_LOCKING; downstream skb_dst_force in
+	 * __xfrm_route_forward then trips its WARN.
+	 *
+	 * Convert any noref dst to refcounted now. Inbound callers
+	 * (xfrm4_rcv_encap_finish, xfrm6_transport_finish2) are inside
+	 * xfrm_input's outer rcu_read_lock so this is safe even when the
+	 * dst is noref. Outbound callers (esp_output_tail_tcp v4/v6) reach
+	 * here with a dst already refcounted by xfrm_output_one, so the
+	 * skb_dst_is_noref(skb) branch inside skb_dst_force() short-circuits
+	 * without invoking dst_hold_safe and the rcu requirement does not
+	 * apply. Same shape as commit 3bc07321ccc2 ("xfrm: Force a dst
+	 * refcount before entering the xfrm type handlers") for the
+	 * analogous crypto-async boundary one layer up.
+	 */
+	skb_dst_force(skb);
+	if (unlikely(!skb_dst(skb)))
+		return -EHOSTUNREACH;
+
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(sizeof(struct xfrm_trans_cb) > sizeof(skb->cb));
 
 	XFRM_TRANS_SKB_CB(skb)->finish = finish;
-- 
2.47.3

